      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Francisco,\n\nAbsolutely, although this patch focuses on providing details about object fields available to build policy rules, I will try to explain the difference between matching \"user.id\" and \"target.user.id\" in a next patch.\n\nBasically, \"user.id\" allows to check the \"user.id\" field of the json message received for a given API call (typically used for a create_user action). On the other hand, \"target.user.id\" allows to check the \"user.id\" field of a user impacted by an API call (the data checked has been loaded from the database) (used for actions involving a user. e.g delete_user).",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAUH/+Y3I\u003d",
      "revId": "3677f7b846bd1dac6f40b4facc5df2346e909c9c",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
